{
  "name": "guard_knife_collapse",
  "note": "(anim-guard) The lethal takedown (BRIEF \"Holding a guard\": the knife at the throat, short and not gratuitous): a short sharp stiffen, then a limp collapse forward and down; no flailing, no hand to the throat. One-shot, 3.0 s (frame i of 48 at i * 3 / 47 s; play the phase min(t / 3, 1) * 47 / 48, never past frame 47). 0-0.2 s the stiffen: the spine arches, the head jerks back, the hands clamp on the arm, up onto the balls of the feet; 0.2-0.35 s held; the holder releases; 0.35-0.7 s the knees buckle and he folds forward, the hands sliding off; 0.7 s the knees reach the floor; 0.7-1.3 s he falls forward from the knees (the knees stay where they landed), the arms limp beside the thighs, the chest and shoulders reaching the floor; 1.3-1.85 s the hips settle forward and down, the legs slide out behind; 1.85-3.0 s lying still face down, the head turned to the side (the pelvis 10 cm off the floor and 0.58 m ahead of the root, the head about 1.27 m ahead: the holder lets go at about 0.35 s). Keys are frames (phase = frame / 48). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up); pelvis offsets in cm from rest (Wren 1.68 m). Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in), wrist { yaw (twist about the forearm), pitch, roll } local to the forearm (anim-rig, RIG.md). Legs (preview and floor checks; the game feet come from the foot planner until a leg channel exists): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up). Keyed by hand from how a real person moves (no game reference); the feet were placed on the floor and the hands on the holder's forearm with a two-bone IK while authoring, then written here as plain angles: edit these numbers directly.",
